  "problem": "| $u$ | $v$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $15$ |\n| $16$ | $20$ |\n| $20$ | $25$ |\n\nThe table above shows a proportional relationship.  Assuming that $v=ku$ for each pair of values, what is the constant of proportionality? \n\nThe constant of proportionality is \n$k=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We're told that $u$ and $v$ have a proportional relationship.\n\nTo find the constant of proportionality, we first need to choose a point $(u,v)$ from the table. Let's choose the point $(12,15),$ which corresponds to the first row of the table.\n\nNow, we can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $v$-coordinate to the $u$-coordinate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{v}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{15÷3}{12÷3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $k=\\frac{5}{4}.$",
